*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Compute the expectation values $chevron.l x chevron.r$, $chevron.l x^2 chevron.r$, $chevron.l p chevron.r$, and $chevron.l p^2 chevron.r$ for the given state.

2. Calculate the uncertainties (standard deviations) using $sigma_x = sqrt(chevron.l x^2 chevron.r - chevron.l x chevron.r^2)$ and $sigma_p = sqrt(chevron.l p^2 chevron.r - chevron.l p chevron.r^2)$.

3. Substitute the calculated uncertainties into the uncertainty product $sigma_x sigma_p$.

4. Verify that the product satisfies the Heisenberg Uncertainty limit $sigma_x sigma_p >= planck/2$.
